    "q-341655": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341655",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(3,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X\\ge 1)=0.8413,$ use the table to find $\\sigma .$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1587\\,$ | $\\,0.1562\\,$ | $\\,0.1539\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1841\\,$ | $\\,0.1814\\,$ | $\\,0.1788\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.2119\\,$ | $\\,0.2090\\,$ | $\\,0.2061\\,$ |\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1) & =P(X<1) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\ge 1) \\\\  & =1-0.8413 \\\\  & =0.1587\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1) & =0.1587 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{1-3}{\\sigma }) & =0.1587 \\\\ Φ\\,(-\\frac{2}{\\sigma }) & =0.1587 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.1587)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.00)=0.1587\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.1587)=-1.00.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & =-1 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
