    "q-341988": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341988",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-1.5<X<1.5)=0.3472,$ use the table to find $\\sigma ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6331\\,$ | $\\,0.6368\\,$ | $\\,0.6406\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6700\\,$ | $\\,0.6736\\,$ | $\\,0.6772\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7054\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ | $\\,0.7123\\,$ |\n\n$\\sigma ≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.5<X<1.5) & =0.3472 \\\\ 2P(0<X<1.5) & =0.3472 \\\\ P(0<X<1.5) & =0.1736 \\\\ P(X<1.5)-P(X<0) & =0.1736 \\\\ P(X<1.5)-0.5 & =0.1736 \\\\ P(X<1.5) & =0.6736 \\\\ P(X\\le 1.5) & =0.6736\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 1.5) & =0.6736 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{1.5-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.6736 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{1.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.6736 \\\\ \\frac{1.5}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.6736)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.45)=0.6736\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.6736)=0.45.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.5}{\\sigma } & =0.45 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.45} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈3.33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
