    "q-342034": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342034",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(|X|<3)=0.5468,$ find ${\\sigma }^{2}.$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8264\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ | $\\,0.8315\\,$ |\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(|X|<3)=P(-3<X<3).\n$$\n\nThen, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-3<X<3) & =0.5468 \\\\ 2P(0<X<3) & =0.5468 \\\\ P(0<X<3) & =0.2734 \\\\ P(X<3)-P(X<0) & =0.2734 \\\\ P(X<3)-0.5 & =0.2734 \\\\ P(X<3) & =0.7734 \\\\ P(X\\le 3) & =0.7734\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =0.7734 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{3-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.7734 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{3}{\\sigma }) & =0.7734 \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7734)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.75)=0.7734\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7734)=0.75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =0.75 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{3}{0.75} \\\\ \\sigma  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =(4)^{2}=16.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
