    "q-94875": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94875",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{3}^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-0.7\\mu <X<2.7\\mu )=0.3256,$ find $\\mu $ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6217\\,$ | $\\,0.6255\\,$ | $\\,0.6293\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6591\\,$ | $\\,0.6628\\,$ | $\\,0.6664\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.6950\\,$ | $\\,0.6985\\,$ | $\\,0.7019\\,$ |\n\n*Hint: Note that the interval $-0.7\\mu <X<2.7\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$*",
      "worked_solution": "Note that we can write the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(\\mu -1.7\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu )=0.3256,\n$$\n\nwhich tells us that the interval $-0.7\\mu <X<2.7\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$\n\nFirst, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mu -1.7\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.3256 \\\\ 2P(\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.3256 \\\\ P(\\mu <X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.1628 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +1.7\\mu )-P(X<\\mu ) & =0.1628 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +1.7\\mu )-0.5 & =0.1628 \\\\ P(X<\\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.6628 \\\\ P(X\\le \\mu +1.7\\mu ) & =0.6628 \\\\ P(X\\le 2.7\\mu ) & =0.6628\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.7\\mu ) & =0.6628 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.7\\mu -\\mu }{3}) & =0.6628 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{1.7\\mu }{3}) & =0.6628 \\\\ \\frac{1.7\\mu }{3} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.6628)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.42)=0.6628\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.6628)=0.42.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.7\\mu }{3} & =0.42 \\\\ 1.7\\mu  & =1.26 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈0.741\\,18 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈0.74.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-94875-a",
