      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(\\mu ,{5}^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-0.8\\mu <X<2.8\\mu )=0.7458,$ find $\\mu ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8485\\,$ | $\\,0.8508\\,$ | $\\,0.8531\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8708\\,$ | $\\,0.8729\\,$ | $\\,0.8749\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8907\\,$ | $\\,0.8925\\,$ | $\\,0.8944\\,$ |\n\n*Hint: Note that the interval $-0.8\\mu <X<2.8\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$*",
      "worked_solution": "Note that we can write the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(\\mu -1.8\\mu <X<\\mu +1.8\\mu )=0.7458,\n$$\n\nwhich tells us that the interval $-0.8\\mu <X<2.8\\mu $ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu .$\n\nFirst, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mu -1.8\\mu <X<\\mu +1.8\\mu ) & =0.7458 \\\\ 2P(\\mu <X<\\mu +1.8\\mu ) & =0.7458 \\\\ P(\\mu <X<2.8\\mu ) & =0.3729 \\\\ P(X<2.8\\mu )-P(X<\\mu ) & =0.3729 \\\\ P(X<2.8\\mu )-0.5 & =0.3729 \\\\ P(X<2.8\\mu ) & =0.8729 \\\\ P(X\\le 2.8\\mu ) & =0.8729\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.8\\mu ) & =0.8729 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.8\\mu -\\mu }{5}) & =0.8729 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{1.8\\mu }{5}) & =0.8729 \\\\ \\frac{1.8\\mu }{5} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.8729)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(1.14)=0.8729\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.8729)=1.14.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.8\\mu }{5} & =1.14 \\\\ 1.8\\mu  & =5.7 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈3.166\\,67 \\\\ \\mu  & ≈3.17.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
